## 12. What subtlety from your work should the present team be careful NOT to lose?

Do not flatten SAT into “GR over QM” or “anti-quantum gravity.”

The sharper SAT claim is subtler:

Fuentes/Penrose ask whether quantum theory should bend toward GR.

SAT asks what happens when GR and ST are treated as orthogonal grammars inside Minkowski geometry, and their intersection is allowed to generate the rest.

Also, do not treat Penrose collapse as either automatically compatible or automatically irrelevant. It is a useful comparator because it targets the same fault line: massive superposition, proper time, and geometry. But SAT probably translates “collapse” into a deeper slice/intersection/constraint phenomenon rather than accepting objective stochastic collapse as primitive.

